// The café's bills – a sibling of cafe.json5 for the one lesson the café's own columns cannot teach:
// clusters that are dense bands rather than round blobs, with scattered cases between them, used by
// the "Density-based clustering" section of docs/en/concepts/clustering.md. The till logged 500 bills
// with the minutes the guest stayed and what they paid. Generated by the exam builder's authored spec
// format (docs/en/exam-spec-reference.md; `proportions` on a group is accepted though that page does
// not list it):
//
//   app-gen --spec docs/examples/cafe-bills.json5 --name cafe-bills --authored
//
// The name is the seed, so `--name cafe-bills` reproduces the dataset exactly; cafe-bills.csv is that
// dataset, written as cafe.csv is. Every number the concept page quotes from it comes from that file,
// so a change to anything here – the name included – is a change to the prose.
// cafe-bills.ru.csv is this dataset with its header (`счёт`, `минуты`, `заказ`) and order labels
// (Drinks «Напитки», Food «Напитки и еда», Other «Прочее») translated, every other value identical –
// the labels sort as the English ones do.
//
// Structure: one factor, Spend, read by `bill`, and one predictor, `minutes` (beta(1.3, 1.3) on 5–60,
// nearly flat), that raises it by 2 factor SDs per predictor SD – the longer a guest stays, the more
// they order. The group `order` shifts Spend by 4.5 SDs per level: Drinks (55% of bills) sit 4.5 SDs
// below Other and Food (39%) 4.5 above, so drinks-only and food bills form two long parallel bands,
// about 4.50 currency units apart at any length of stay and about 0.50 thick, bending a little at the shortest and
// longest stays (the predictor's margin is not normal). Other (6%) – a group's whole order paid by one
// guest, a staff meal, a cake taken home – sits between them with 8 times the spread, scattered across
// the plane. The bands are long against the gap between them, so k-means at k = 2 cuts both across
// rather than along; DBSCAN and HDBSCAN follow each band and leave most of the Other bills that miss
// the bands as noise. n = 500 is the size at which this realization gives both density methods the two
// bands cleanly; at 400 HDBSCAN broke off the short-stay end of the drinks band.
// No missing data and no deliberate flaws.
{
	n: 500,
	factors: ["Spend"],
	variables: {
		bill: { load: "Spend*0.99", family: "normal", params: [11.25, 0.5], round: 2 },
	},
	groups: {
		order: { levels: ["Drinks", "Other", "Food"], proportions: [0.55, 0.06, 0.39], effect: "Spend*4.5", spread: [1, 8, 1] },
	},
	predictors: {
		minutes: { family: "beta", params: [1.3, 1.3], min: 5, max: 60, round: 0, effect: "Spend*2" },
	},
}
